@startuml fr06-distraction
' Origin: drafted with AI assistance (Claude Code) from FR-06 in docs/02-requirements.md; reviewed by the author.
title FR-06 Log a distraction
|Student|
start
:POST /sessions/{id}/distractions\n{type, optional site, optional note};
|Focus|
if (session exists and is the student's?) then (no)
  :404;
  stop
elseif (session still active?) then (no)
  :409;
  stop
elseif (type known (case-insensitive), site ≤ 200, note ≤ 500?) then (no)
  :400;
  stop
else (ok)
endif
if (site given?) then (yes)
  :Clean site to a host\n(no scheme, www., port, path);
  if (host or a parent domain is allowed?) then (yes)
    :offPolicy = false;
  else (no)
    :offPolicy = true;
  endif
else (no)
  :offPolicy = false;
endif
:Add Distraction (time = server clock);
:Save, publish **DistractionLogged** → focus.distractions\n(the note stays in Focus);
:201;
|Focus streams|
:Count it in the spike window (FR-12);
stop
@enduml
